WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  now back in washington the white house  is clarifying an off-the-cuff remark u.s  president joe biden made during a speech  in poland seeming to suggest it was time  for the russians to force president  vladimir putin out  for god's sake this man cannot remain  power the comment seemed to be a direct  call for regime change in russia white  house officials were quick to clear up  any confusion we do not have a strategy  of regime change in russia or anywhere  else for that matter it's up to the  people of the country in question it's  up to  the russian people the president did  extend an olive branch to the russian  people telling them they are not the  enemy the kremlin shot back saying it's  up to russian citizens to elect their  president but under putin's rule  elections have not been fair or free his  political opponents are often jailed or  silenced although some world leaders  believe this war could cost putin his  job the russian people i think are  pretty fed up  with what is happening  in ukraine this illegal invasion  the destruction of their own livelihoods  their economy  is collapsing around them before and  during the war the u.s has repeatedly  asked putin to come to the negotiating  table find a diplomatic way out  while france's president is calling for  this situation not to get out of control  others believe putin won't forget what  biden said it will play on his mind and  it could complicate matters going down  the road  still others say biden was just voicing  the hopes of millions around the world i  think many people will sympathize with  the sentiments  that led him to say what he did for now  the white house is sticking to its  statement that the u.s will not be  involved in any regime change in russia  instead the administration is moving  ahead with its strategy of cutting off  putin his billionaire backers and the  russian economy from the rest of the  world  jennifer johnson global news washington

